During the ten days of Onam, families make a pookalam, a carpet of flower petals, at their doorstep. It grows larger each day. On Thiruvonam, the main day, they serve the Onasadya, a feast of often more than 20 dishes on a [[@south-indian-meals|banana leaf]], from banana chips to several kinds of payasam, a sweet pudding. It's a bit like a [[@thali|thali]] laid out on a leaf.

In the backwaters of [[@kerala|Kerala]], snake boat races, called vallam kali, are held around Onam. Each long, narrow boat carries dozens of rowers pulling in [[rhythm|rhythm]]. The Nehru Trophy Boat Race on Punnamada Lake, near Alappuzha, began after Jawaharlal Nehru's visit in 1952.

